Z||000000||fiero56||01-09-2001||09:28 PM||||I am still looking for information on changing the gear ratios of the Isuzu tranny. Either books, or websites, or anyone who knows the Isuzu tranny well. I need info on opening the case, diagrams of the innards, and info relating on matching gear sets to engine performance and power bands.<P>Post 1900!<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||01-10-2001||11:08 AM||||Congrats on post 1900. I also want info on the izusu. I love mine hooked to my v6. I would love to play with the final drive ratio.<P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||01-10-2001||12:56 PM||||56,<P>We are on the same track.  Check out <A HREF="http://www.isuzuperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.isuzuperformance.com</A>   They have some really cool stuff on that site (i.e. the VW 02A 6 spd conversion and Quaife diff's.) I e-mailed Bill during the holidays but never received a reply.  You might want to call him.  If you do, ask him what bhp/torque they can withstand reliably driven moderately.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000003||Shaun41178||01-10-2001||02:59 PM||||Email Mike Lecompte at Hyptnotise@aol.com  he has a customs 3.83 final drive that he is installing behind his race prepped V6.  Should give awesome off line acceleration and amazing top end too.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Chris McDonald||01-10-2001||04:12 PM||||It is either the Chilton or Haines manual that actually has a break down of the trans.  I have been inside one myself.  If you are very careful to lay out the parts in the order you pulled them you will be able to get it back together.  The manual was a huge help to me.  <P>I don't know anything about changing the final drive.  <P>Have fun.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lou_dias||01-11-2001||02:52 PM||||I guess you guys want to go higher with your geering, not me... Give me a getrag from a Cavalier with a 3.42 final drive and I'll give you a 1/2 second quicker 0-60 time and a .1 sec slower quarter mile time any day...<BR>Why is it 1/2 second quicker to 60?  Cause you are still in second gear and don't waste time shifting into 3rd.<P>A long time ago, I read where a guy put in the 3.23 final drive into a getrag for a Lambo conversion with a v8 to gain acceptable fuel ecomony.  I think final drive gears are very interchangeable on these transmissions.  Curious as to the gears on the new Getrag that's in the Sunfires and Grand Am's...  Anybody know?||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||01-11-2001||04:23 PM||||Actually, I'm looking to go lower. The stock Fiero Getrag(what my Formula has right now)has a 3.61 final drive(it will hit 60mph in second gear BTW). But, I am also not pleased with the huge drop from 3.50 in first to 2.05 into second. <BR>That's why I am planning for a Fiero Isuzu with 3.35FD. But, to compensate for the FD, GM put in higer gearing for all gears except second(2nd in Isuzu is 2.04).<P>I love the Muncie 4-speed, and wouldn't hesitate to put one in, but it lacks a nice highway cruising gear. The reason for my search to get the Isuzu gearing near the Muncie, but then add a nice highway gear.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jimmy||01-12-2001||02:00 AM||||     Not to get to off topic but can you take the axle ratio out of a cavalier or similar car and just swap it into a fiero getrag tranny?  Last time I checked the specs on my g/r and such, my 87 GT has a first gear of 3.92 and an axle ratio of 3.61!  Thats about the worst tranny to have in my 87 GT with the V8.  First gear will be useless.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Anybody whos done this? TIA<P>Jim <BR>87 GT T-TOP V8<BR>87 GT||||reg||1
